.TH LIBREWING-TOOL 1 "September 2026" "LibreWing 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
librewing-tool \- inspect and maintain LibreWing
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B librewing-tool
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B health
Check required commands, configured listeners, and the active SIP003 plugin.
.TP
.B config-path
Print the application configuration path.
.TP
.B log-path
Print the proxy log path.
.TP
.B show-profile
Print the active profile with its password redacted. Use
.B --json
for JSON output.
.TP
.B show-url --unsafe
Print the credential-bearing ss:// URL for the active profile.
.TP
.BI "qr-export " output
Export the active profile as a private PNG QR code.
.TP
.BI "qr-import " image
Import the first ss:// QR code found in an image.
.TP
.BI "backup-export " output
Export all settings and server profiles to an owner-only JSON file.
.TP
.BI "backup-import " input " --yes"
Replace local settings from a backup after explicit confirmation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR librewing (1),
.BR ss-local (1)
.SH SECURITY
Profile URLs, QR images, and backups contain server credentials. Do not publish
them in issue reports or logs.
